<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<PathAssistant xmlns="http://soap.sforce.com/2006/04/metadata">
    <!--
        DEACTIVATED 2026-08-09, NOT DELETED, AND THAT IS DELIBERATE.

        LOI__c gained two record types in this tranche (Acquisition_LOI, Disposition_LOI). A
        Path is configured PER RECORD TYPE, and recordTypeName CANNOT BE RE-POINTED on an
        existing PathAssistant - so this __MASTER__ path is superseded by two new files,
        LOI_Path_Acquisition and LOI_Path_Disposition, exactly as Tranche 2 superseded
        Disposition_Path and 3A superseded NDA_Path.

        It is retained rather than deleted because it is the record of the guidance text the
        acquisition steps were copied from. LOI_Path_Acquisition carries all five <info> texts
        BYTE-IDENTICAL to the steps below, and like this file it declares no <fieldNames> on
        any step - that absence was copied forward too, rather than being "improved", because
        adding key fields would change what an acquisition user sees on a live path for no
        requested reason.

        Once record types exist, a __MASTER__ path renders for the Master type only - which
        after the row migration is NO ROWS. Leaving it active would therefore do nothing useful
        and would make the Path configuration ambiguous to the next reader.

        ORDER OF OPERATIONS AT DEPLOY: profile record-type assignment and the migration of every
        existing LOI row off Master to Acquisition_LOI must both complete BEFORE the two new
        paths are relied on, for the same reason Tranche 2's gate A2 exists - a row still on
        Master matches no record-type Path and renders a Path with no current position.
    -->
    <active>false</active>
    <entityName>LOI__c</entityName>
    <fieldName>Stage__c</fieldName>
    <masterLabel>LOI Path</masterLabel>
    <pathAssistantSteps>
        <info>LOI finalized and complete. Record is closed out for this stage of the deal.</info>
        <picklistValueName>Completed</picklistValueName>
    </pathAssistantSteps>
    <pathAssistantSteps>
        <info>Counter-offer stage. Track the back-and-forth with the seller - log each counter in the Counter History and update the offer terms until both sides align.</info>
        <picklistValueName>Counter</picklistValueName>
    </pathAssistantSteps>
    <pathAssistantSteps>
        <info>Draft the letter of intent - capture the offer price, cap rate and key terms. Keep it here until the draft is ready for internal review.</info>
        <picklistValueName>Draft</picklistValueName>
    </pathAssistantSteps>
    <pathAssistantSteps>
        <info>Prepare and review the LOI internally. Validate the terms, route it for any required approval, and refine based on feedback before finalizing.</info>
        <picklistValueName>Prepare/Review</picklistValueName>
    </pathAssistantSteps>
    <pathAssistantSteps>
        <info>LOI sent to the seller/broker. Awaiting their response - a counter moves it to the Counter stage.</info>
        <picklistValueName>Sent</picklistValueName>
    </pathAssistantSteps>
    <recordTypeName>__MASTER__</recordTypeName>
</PathAssistant>
